.claude
.kiro
.agents
node_modules

# ── Secrets: MUST stay excluded ────────────────────────────────────────────────
# `gcloud builds submit` uploads the working directory into a Cloud Build GCS
# source bucket. Because a .gcloudignore FILE EXISTS, gcloud does NOT fall back
# to .gitignore patterns at all, and there is no `#!include:.gitignore` directive
# here -- so .env files were being uploaded despite being git-ignored.
#
# services/mobile-api/.env holds a live SUPABASE_SERVICE_ROLE_KEY, MAPBOX_ACCESS_TOKEN,
# OPENAI_API_KEY and CRON_SECRET. The Dockerfile's `COPY services/mobile-api
# services/mobile-api` (line 22) pulled it into the builder stage too; the runtime
# stage only copies dist/, so the shipped IMAGE was clean, but the secret still
# transited and is retained in the source bucket.
#
# The build does not need any of these: runtime config comes from Cloud Run env
# vars. Found by the 2026-09-25 triage as P0-5
# (docs/plans/external-review-triage-2026-09-25.md).
.env
.env.*
**/.env
**/.env.*
*.jks
*.keystore
*.p8
*.p12
*.pem
*-service-account*.json
*serviceaccount*.json
# ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Mobile app source — Dockerfile only needs apps/mobile/package.json, but
# excluding the whole directory breaks that COPY. Exclude heavy subtrees only.
apps/mobile/android
apps/mobile/ios
apps/mobile/.expo
apps/mobile/app
apps/mobile/src
apps/mobile/assets
apps/mobile/__tests__
apps/web
packages/core/dist
dist
output
tmp
# Release artefacts (each AAB/APK is 100–200 MB; pre-fix tarballs were ~1 GB)
*.apk
*.aab
*.docx
apkreleases/
LaunchPR/
docs/
design-work/
